            {
              "id": "dce2f52",
              "elType": "widget",
              "settings": {
                "editor": "<p>Deccan Birders was founded in 1980 as the Birdwatchers' Society of Andhra Pradesh (BSAP), born out of a\nsmall group of enthusiasts who met on weekends to record the birds of Hyderabad's lakes and scrublands.\nWhat began as informal outings soon grew into a structured society with a shared mission: to document,\ncelebrate, and protect the avifauna of the Deccan Plateau.</p>\n<p>In 1984, the society launched PITTA, its monthly newsletter, giving members a place to share sightings,\ntrip reports, and articles on bird behaviour and conservation. Over the following decades, Deccan Birders\norganised the region's first waterfowl censuses, contributed field data to national ornithological surveys,\nand built one of the most active birdwatching communities in South India.</p>\n<p>Following the bifurcation of Andhra Pradesh in 2014, the society was renamed Deccan Birders to reflect its\nregional identity and continuing focus on the plateau's birdlife. Today, with more than 570 members, a\npacked calendar of field trips and talks, and an unbroken 45-year publishing record, Deccan Birders remains\ncommitted to its founding purpose — spreading the message of bird conservation.</p>",
                "typography_typography": "custom",
                "typography_font_family": "Source Sans 3",
                "typography_font_size": {
                  "unit": "px",
                  "size": 16,
                  "sizes": []
                }
